 [05] baseline - hash the default-param render and keep a copy to A/B listen
 canvas-render.wav MISSING - step 04 did not write; step 07 will say CANNOT-CHECK.
 " "
 [06] WINDOW SESSION - the window opens when you press a key. In it:
 A. long-press the EMPTY canvas - tap ADD MODULE - type sine on the
 keyboard - tap the Sine row. A Sine node appears where you pressed.
 B. tap the new Sine node - the INSPECTOR shows Frequency and
 Amplitude - drag the Frequency slider. The value follows your
 finger; the log band reports Frequency = ... Hz when you lift.
 C. long-press the empty canvas - tap RENDER WAV. This overwrites
 canvas-render.wav WITH YOUR EDIT - step [07] hashes it.
 D. drag the small ring near a wire END onto another port - the wire
 moves. Three-finger tap - it returns, same wire.
 E. three-finger tap again - the slider drag undoes, value returns.
 F. long-press a NODE - tap RENAME - type a name - press ENTER:
 the header shows it. Three-finger tap: the old name is back.
 Reopen RENAME, press ESC or tap outside: cancels, name kept.
 G. add a Mixer via the browser, tap it: 20 rows, the last ones
 clipped. Two-finger drag UP inside the panel: the rows scroll,
 the thin thumb at the right edge moves, the CANVAS does not.
 H. bypass a node from its menu, then pinch two fingers together
 on the canvas to zoom out: first the boxes lose ALL text -
 states ride patterns now: hatched body = bypassed, dashed
 border = muted, double border = locked, header chip = master.
 Pinch further: dots and HAIRLINE wires; the bypassed dot is a
 hollow ring. Compare with design\mockups\design-mode.svg and
 write what differs into the H answer below.
 I. wire the thesis chain: spawn an SVF via the browser, drag
 gain OUT to svf IN, drag rms LEVEL to svf CUTOFF-MOD, then
 long-press empty canvas - RENDER WAV. The cyan cv wire lights
 from the rms value; the audio wires light as before.
 J. LIVE AUDIO, the WO-012 inc2 acceptance: tap PLAY on the rail.
 The log names the backend, the NEGOTIATED rate and the latency;
 you HEAR the patch through the device - shared mode, about
 22.67 ms - and the wires animate CONTINUOUSLY from the engine's
 own meters while it plays, not only after RENDER WAV.
 K. while it plays: drag a slider - the sound changes LIVE, no stop,
 no click at the moment of the edit; drag a new wire - it goes
 audible at the next block boundary. Tap STOP: sound stops and
 the evidence line names blocks, xruns, swaps and allocations.
 WITH A MOUSE, if one is handy: right-click a node opens its menu
 where a finger long-presses; the wheel scrolls the inspector over
 the panel and pans the canvas over the canvas; plain hover is
 silent. Write what felt wrong into the K answer too.
 OPTIONAL, only with a spare cable: unplug the output device
 mid-play - one honest Removed line, the session ends, and the
 canvas is untouched. Write what you heard into the J/K answers.
 Then close the window; the script continues by itself.
 Over RDP the rasteriser is WARP - slow but functional; the 60 fps
 claim waits for the physical screen, as always.
